A||||3||mshill||Rim and wheel questions...||||5||
Z||000000||mshill||05-28-2000||01:08 PM||||Are the stock GT rims 15x7 or 15x8?<P>What is the widest tire you can put on a 15x8 rim?||||reg||5
Z||000001||2birds||05-28-2000||01:26 PM||||15x7 for 86-87 GT, I'm not positive, but I believe the fronts were 15x6 on the 88 GT/Formula, due to the new front suspension.  Easy to spot, since they have no dish to them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-28-2000||03:43 PM||||I'm not certain but I think '87 & '88 GT's came out with 15x6 front and 15x7 rears. My '87 GT had aftermaket rims when I got it so I'm not sure on the '87. The '88 GT definatley had that config. though.<P>There is a ton of tire threads if you search for them. <P>I have Goodyear Eagle HP, 215/60/15's on 15x6 on my '87 GT at the moment. They work great on the '87. They SUCK on my '88 Coupe. They '88 Coupe seems to profer the 215/60/14 'S' rated tires that I got from my parts car...Go figure. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||05-28-2000||04:00 PM||||I've left the tire sizes stock on my 88 Formula... 205X60R15 front and 215/60R15 rear.  They are Dunlop D60 A2's.  I had some wider tires on the front for a while, but went back to the stock size.  The car steers better with the smaller tires.  I decided it took too much muscle to go around corners and through traffic in the mostly city driving that I do.||||reg||1
